{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 5 absent, fewer paths feed the output, so adding a direct 3x3 conv from the input to the output adds more capacity and signal flow."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when edge 3 is also empty cuts most of the paths into the output, so the drop in accuracy is larger."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 receives no input, so a conv on edge 4 (node 1 to node 3) processes nothing and gives little benefit."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learnable 3x3 conv on the last edge with parameter-free pooling loses more than replacing a skip connection does."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for pooling removes capacity, whereas swapping a skip for pooling changes little."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Putting a skip on an empty edge adds a useful path, while replacing a 3x3 conv with a skip removes capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv to an empty edge into the output gains more than upgrading an edge that already holds a 1x1 conv, skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the residual skip from the input to the output hurts trainability more than removing other operations from that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Feeding node 1 with a conv matters more when node 1 connects to the output through a conv on edge 4."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual skip where the direct edge is empty helps more than replacing an existing conv or pool on that edge."}], "tok": 30000, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x